{"id":"4ccdb474528397f5f84fc3c1046ecc2cbefba667","axis":"silent","repo":"envoyproxy/envoy","sha":"4ccdb474528397f5f84fc3c1046ecc2cbefba667","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"api/envoy/extensions/filters/http/ext_authz/v3/ext_authz.proto","lines":["@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ option (udpa.annotations.file_status).package_version_status = ACTIVE;"," // External Authorization :ref:`configuration overview <config_http_filters_ext_authz>`."," // [#extension: envoy.filters.http.ext_authz]"," ","-// [#next-free-field: 35]","+// [#next-free-field: 36]"," message ExtAuthz {","   option (udpa.annotations.versioning).previous_message_type =","       \"envoy.config.filter.http.ext_authz.v3.ExtAuthz\";","@@ -317,6 +317,26 @@ message ExtAuthz {","   // It is set to ``false`` by default for backwards compatibility.","   bool encode_raw_headers = 23;"," ","+  // Whether to read header values from :ref:`HeaderValue.raw_value","+  // <envoy_v3_api_field_config.core.v3.HeaderValue.raw_value>` in gRPC authorization responses","+  // (:ref:`CheckResponse <envoy_v3_api_msg_service.auth.v3.CheckResponse>`).","+  //","+  // When set to ``true``, each header value in gRPC ``OK``, ``denied``, and ``error`` responses is","+  // read from ``HeaderValue.raw_value`` when non-empty, falling back to","+  // :ref:`HeaderValue.value <envoy_v3_api_field_config.core.v3.HeaderValue.value>` when","+  // ``raw_value`` is empty. This allows gRPC authorization servers to return non-UTF-8 header","+  // values while remaining compatible with servers that populate ``value``.","+  //","+  // When set to ``false``, only ``HeaderValue.value`` is read and ``HeaderValue.raw_value`` is","+  // ignored.","+  //","+  // .. note::","+  //   This field applies exclusively to the gRPC ext_authz service and has no effect on the HTTP","+  //   service.","+  //","+  // Defaults to ``false``.","+  bool read_raw_header_value = 35;","+","   // Rules for what modifications an ext_authz server may make to the request headers before","   // continuing decoding or forwarding upstream.","   //","@@ -451,7 +471,10 @@ message ShadowDecision {"," ","   // Response headers the auth server asked to set on a denied response","   // (e.g. ``WWW-Authenticate``, ``Set-Cookie``). Populated for ``DENIED`` only.","-  // Preserves ordering and duplicate header names.","+  // Preserves ordering and duplicate header names. For each header,","+  // :ref:`value <envoy_v3_api_field_config.core.v3.HeaderValue.value>` is populated for valid","+  // UTF-8 values, and :ref:`raw_value","+  // <envoy_v3_api_field_config.core.v3.HeaderValue.raw_value>` is populated for non-UTF-8 values.","   repeated config.core.v3.HeaderValue response_headers = 3;"," }"," "],"additions":25,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"api/envoy/service/auth/v3/external_auth.proto","lines":["@@ -54,6 +54,12 @@ message DeniedHttpResponse {","   // false when used in this message.","   // The :ref:`keep_empty_value field in HeaderValueOption <envoy_v3_api_field_config.core.v3.HeaderValueOption.keep_empty_value>`","   // is not supported.","+  // When :ref:`read_raw_header_value","+  // <envoy_v3_api_field_extensions.filters.http.ext_authz.v3.ExtAuthz.read_raw_header_value>` is","+  // set to ``true``, each header value is read from :ref:`HeaderValue.raw_value","+  // <envoy_v3_api_field_config.core.v3.HeaderValue.raw_value>` when non-empty, falling back to","+  // :ref:`HeaderValue.value <envoy_v3_api_field_config.core.v3.HeaderValue.value>` when","+  // ``raw_value`` is empty. Otherwise, only ``HeaderValue.value`` is read.","   repeated config.core.v3.HeaderValueOption headers = 2;"," ","   // This field allows the authorization service to send a response body data","@@ -76,6 +82,12 @@ message OkHttpResponse {","   // one if there is a match.","   // The :ref:`keep_empty_value field in HeaderValueOption <envoy_v3_api_field_config.core.v3.HeaderValueOption.keep_empty_value>`","   // is not supported.","+  // When :ref:`read_raw_header_value","+  // <env